# gamified3D overview

A UI/UX framework for 2.5D game-style interfaces on three.js. Companion to gamifiedUI
(c:\Users\kason\Desktop\gamifiedUI): gamifiedUI owns CSS components (HUD, panels, icons and
CSS-only `gx-iso` scenes); gamified3D owns the WebGL stage those components sit on. Never put CSS
components here, and never put three.js code in gamifiedUI.

Scope is interface building blocks (stage, grid, interaction, anchors, motion, camera controls,
accessibility), not game content. Terrain, characters and world simulation do not belong here.

## Layout (npm workspaces)

- `packages/*` - one package per module, each with its own `LICENSE`, `NOTICE` and `CHANGELOG.md`.
- `three` is a peer dependency of every package, never bundled.

## Design contract

- Modules are framework-agnostic and hold no game logic; hosts pass state in and get events out.
- Every interaction works with pointer, touch and keyboard alone; gamepad is additive.
- Interactive 3D objects have a DOM counterpart for focus order and screen readers.
- Motion reads gamifiedUI's motion tokens and stops under `prefers-reduced-motion` and
  `data-gx-motion="reduce"`.
- DOM overlays use gamifiedUI classes and themes, so the stage and the HUD match.

## Commands (PowerShell; no `&&` chaining in docs)

- `npm install`.
